notes.ai — running assistant notes (user-managed)
====================================================


2026-01-20
- Added boot intro animation: rapid falling tetrominoes that fill the 16x16 matrix (skippable via any input).
  Config: INTRO_ENABLED / INTRO_MAX_MS / INTRO_FRAME_MS / INTRO_MAX_FRAMES_PER_PIECE.
- Implemented Serial-open dim mode with smooth brightness fades:
  - Default BRIGHTNESS=95 (USB charger).
  - When USB-CDC Serial is opened, target becomes USB_BRIGHTNESS_WHEN_HOST=15 (optional latch).
  - Fade timings: BRIGHTNESS_FADE_UP_MS / BRIGHTNESS_FADE_DOWN_MS.
- New artifact: tetris-main-serial-dim-v10-intro-dropfill-fade.zip

- Set BRIGHTNESS to 95 to match charger target (full brightness).

- v10c: Fix build error in intro (min() type mismatch) by replacing with uint32_t-safe ternary holdEnd computation.

- v10d: Fix linker error by adding missing MatrixDisplay::tickPowerBrightness() implementation (Serial-open dim + fade engine) to display_matrix_core.cpp.

2026-01-20
- v11: Intro is longer, speeds up over time (ramped frame delay + frames-per-piece), and ends with a 'bang' (white flashes + expanding ring) before clearing to game.

2026-01-20
- v12: Added big scrolling marquee title intro (default text "TETRIS" at scale 2) before dropfill intro; added BOOT_STATS_ENABLED (default false) to skip MAX level boot stats.

2026-01-20
- v12b: Fix build: remove duplicate config.h defines (fade macros, etc.) and repair main.cpp preprocessor gating (remove stray #endif) for BOOT_STATS_ENABLED.

2026-01-21
- v13: Made the in-game "level number drop-down" overlay optional via LEVEL_NUMBER_DROPDOWN_ENABLED (default false).

2026-01-21
- v14: Added a border-only "decade milestone" reveal animation when entering levels 11/21/31/... (new 10-level border style).
